# Trivy Ignore File for Known Base Image Vulnerabilities
# https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# CVE-2023-45853: zlib integer overflow
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Status: will_not_fix by Debian
# Reason: This vulnerability is in the base Debian image's zlib package.
#         Debian security team has marked this as will_not_fix for Bookworm.
#         The vulnerability requires specific attack conditions that are
#         unlikely in containerized .NET applications.
# Mitigation: Using slim images and latest patches. Monitoring for updates.
CVE-2023-45853

# CVE-2023-2953: OpenLDAP null pointer dereference
# Severity: HIGH  
# Status: affected in Debian 12 (Bookworm)
# Reason: This is in libldap-2.5-0 from base image. The application does not
#         directly use LDAP functionality, reducing attack surface.
# Mitigation: Using slim images. Will update when patched version available.
CVE-2023-2953

# CVE-2025-6020: Linux-PAM directory traversal
# Severity: HIGH
# Status: Recently disclosed, patch pending
# Reason: This is in libpam-modules from base image. The application runs as
#         non-root user with limited permissions, mitigating impact.
# Mitigation: Using non-root user in containers. Monitoring for updates.
CVE-2025-6020

# Note: This file should be reviewed regularly (weekly/monthly) to:
# 1. Check if patches have been released for ignored CVEs
# 2. Remove entries when vulnerabilities are fixed
# 3. Update base images to incorporate security patches
# 4. Ensure ignored CVEs don't pose unacceptable risk to the application
